# Netlify reads this from the deploy root (public/ ships verbatim into out/).
#
# The site this one replaces served its pages as .html files. Permanent
# redirects carry those addresses — and whatever search standing they have —
# over to the new pages instead of letting them fall into a 404. None of these
# files exist in the export, so the rules can never shadow a real page.
/terms.html      /terms/     301
/privacy.html    /privacy/   301
/discover.html   /discover/  301
